  "title": "78: al-Nabaa النبإ",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nعَمَّ يَتَسَآءَلُوْنَۚ‏(1)\nA’MMA YATA-SAAA-ALOON.\nWhat is it that they are questioning each other about?!\nعَنِ النَّبَاِ الْعَظِيْمِۙ‏(2)\nA’NIN NABA-IL A’ZEEMIL\n[Is it] about the Great Tiding,\nالَّذِىْ هُمْ فِيْهِ مُخْتَلِفُوْنَؕ‏(3)\nLAZEE HUM FEEHE MUKHTALEFOON.\nthe one about which they differ?\nكَلَّا سَيَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(4)\nKALLAA SA-YA’LAMOONA.\nNo indeed! Soon they will know!\nثُمَّ كَلَّا سَيَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(5)\nSUMMA KALLAA SAYA’LAMOON.\nNo indeed! Soon they will know for once again!\nاَلَمْ نَجْعَلِ الْاَرْضَ مِهٰدًا ۙ‏(6)\nALAM NAJ-A’LIL ARZA MEHAADANW.\nDid We not make the earth a resting place?\nوَّالْجِبَالَ اَوْتَادًا ۙ‏(7)\nWAL JEBAALA AWTAADANW\nand the mountains stakes?\nوَّخَلَقْنٰكُمْ اَزْوَاجًا ۙ‏(8)\nWA KHALAQNAAKUM AZWAAJANW.\nand create you in pairs?\nوَّجَعَلْنَا نَوْمَكُمْ سُبَاتًا ۙ‏(9)\nWA JA-A’LNAA NAWMAKUM SOBAATANW.\nand make your sleep for rest?\nوَّجَعَلْنَا الَّيْلَ لِبَاسًا ۙ‏(10)\nWA JA-A’LNAL LAYLA LEBAASANW.\nand make the night a covering?\nوَّجَعَلْنَا النَّهَارَ مَعَاشًا‏(11)\nWA JA-A’LNAN NAHAARA MA-A’ASHANW.\nand make the day for livelihood?\nوَّبَنَيْنَا فَوْقَكُمْ سَبْعًا شِدَادًا ۙ‏(12)\nWA BANAYNAA FAWQAKUM SAB-A’N SHEDAADANW.\nand build above you the seven mighty heavens?\nوَّ جَعَلْنَا سِرَاجًا وَّهَّاجًا ۙ‏(13)\nWA JA-A’LNAA SERAAJANW WAH-HAAJANW.\nand make [the sun for] a radiant lamp?\nوَّاَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ الْمُعْصِرٰتِ مَآءً ثَجَّاجًا ۙ‏(14)\nWA ANZALNAA MENAL MO’SERAATE MAAA-AN SAJJAAJAL.\nand send down water pouring from the rain-clouds,\nلِّنُخْرِجَ بِهٖ حَبًّا وَّنَبَاتًا ۙ‏(15)\nLE-NUKHREJA BEHI HABBANW WA NABAATANW\nthat We may bring forth with it grains and plants,\nوَّجَنّٰتٍ اَلْفَافًا ؕ‏(16)\nWA JANNAATIN ALFAAFAA.\nand luxuriant gardens?\nاِنَّ يَوْمَ الْفَصْلِ كَانَ مِيْقَاتًا ۙ‏(17)\nINNA YAWMAL FASLE KAANA MEEQAATANY.\nIndeed the Day of Judgement is the tryst,\nيَّوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِى الصُّوْرِ فَتَاْتُوْنَ اَفْوَاجًا ۙ‏(18)\nYAWMA TUNFAKHO FIS SOORE FA-TAATOONA AFWAAJANW.\nthe day the Trumpet will be blown, and you will come in groups,\nوَّفُتِحَتِ السَّمَآءُ فَكَانَتْ اَبْوَابًا ۙ‏(19)\nWA FOTEHATIS SAMAAA-O FA KAANAT ABWAABANW.\nand the sky will be opened and become gates,\nوَّ سُيِّرَتِ الْجِبَالُ فَكَانَتْ سَرَابًا ؕ‏(20)\nWA SUYYERATIL JEBAALO FA KAANAT SARAABAA.\nand the mountains will be set moving and become a mirage.\nاِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ كَانَتْ مِرْصَادًا ۙ‏(21)\nINNA JAHANNAMA KAANAT MIRSAADAL.\nIndeed hell is in ambush,\nلِّلطّٰغِيْنَ مَاٰبًا ۙ‏(22)\nLIT-TAAGHEENA MA-AABAL.\na resort for the rebels,\nلّٰبِثِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَحْقَابًا ۚ‏(23)\nLAABESEENA FEEHAA AHQAABAA.\nto reside therein for ages,\nلَا يَذُوْقُوْنَ فِيْهَا بَرْدًا وَّلَا شَرَابًا ۙ‏(24)\nLAA YAZOOQOONA FEEHAA BARDANW WA LAA SHARAABAA.\ntasting in it neither any coolness nor drink,\nاِلَّا حَمِيْمًا وَّغَسَّاقًا ۙ‏(25)\nILLAA HAMEEMANW WA GHASSAAQAA.\nexcept boiling water and pus,\nجَزَآءً وِّفَاقًا ؕ‏(26)\nJA-ZAAA-ANW WEFAAQAA.\na fitting requital.\nاِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا لَا يَرْجُوْنَ حِسَابًا ۙ‏(27)\nINNAHUM KAANOO LAA YARJOONA HESAABANW.\nIndeed they did not expect any reckoning,\nوَّكَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا كِذَّابًا ؕ‏(28)\nWA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA KIZZAABAA.\nand they denied Our signs mendaciously,\nوَكُلَّ شَىْءٍ اَحْصَيْنٰهُ كِتٰبًا ۙ‏(29)\nWA KULLA SHAY-IN AHSAYNAAHO KETAABAA.\nand We have figured everything in a Book.\nفَذُوْقُوْا فَلَنْ نَّزِيْدَكُمْ اِلَّا عَذَابًا‏(30)\nFA-ZOOQOO FALAN NAZEEDAKUM ILLAA A’ZAABAA.\nSo [now] taste! We shall increase you in nothing but punishment!\nاِنَّ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ مَفَازًا ۙ‏(31)\nINNA LIL MUTTAQEENA MAFAAZAA.\nIndeed a triumph awaits the Godwary:\nحَدَآئِقَ وَاَعْنَابًا ۙ‏(32)\nHADAAA-EQA WA A-A’NAABANW\ngardens and vineyards,\nوَّكَوَاعِبَ اَتْرَابًا ۙ‏(33)\nWA KAWAA-E’BA ATRAABANW.\nand buxom maidens of a like age,\nوَّكَاْسًا دِهَاقًا ؕ‏(34)\nWA KAASAN DEHAAQAA.\nand brimming cups.\nلَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ فِيْهَا لَغْوًا وَّلَا كِذّٰبًا ۚ‏(35)\nLAA YAS-MA-O’ONA FEEHAA LAGHWANW WA LAA KIZZAABAA.\nTherein they shall hear neither vain talk nor lies\nجَزَآءً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ عَطَآءً حِسَابًا ۙ‏(36)\nJA-ZAAA-AM MIR RABBEKA A’TAAA-AN HESAABAR.\n—a reward and a sufficing bounty from your Lord,\nرَّبِّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا الرَّحْمٰنِ لَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ مِنْهُ خِطَابًا ۚ‏(37)\nRABBIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAR RAHMAANE LAA YAMLEKOONA MINHO KHETAABAA.\nthe All-beneficent, the Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them. They will not be able to address Him\nيَوْمَ يَقُوْمُ الرُّوْحُ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ صَفًّا ؕۙ لَّا يَتَكَلَّمُوْنَ اِلَّا مَنْ اَذِنَ لَهُ الرَّحْمٰنُ وَقَالَ صَوَابًا‏(38)\nYAWMA YAQOOMUR ROOHO WAL MALAAA-EKATO SAFFAL, LAA YATAKALLAMOONA ILLAA MAN AZENA LAHUR RAHMAANO WA QAALA SAWAABAA.\non the day when the Spirit and the angels stand in an array: none shall speak except someone who is permitted by the All-beneficent and says what is rightful.\nذٰلِكَ الْيَوْمُ الْحَقُّ ۚ فَمَنْ شَآءَ اتَّخَذَ اِلٰى رَبِّهٖ مَاٰبًا‏(39)\nZAALEKAL YAWMUL HAQQ, FAMAN SHAAA-AT TAKHAZA ELAA RABBEHI MA-AABAA.\nThat day is true for certain. So let anyone who wishes take resort with his Lord.\nاِنَّاۤ اَنْذَرْنٰكُمْ عَذَابًا قَرِيْبًا ۖۚ  يَّوْمَ يَنْظُرُ الْمَرْءُ مَا قَدَّمَتْ يَدٰهُ وَيَقُوْلُ الْكٰفِرُ يٰلَيْتَنِىْ كُنْتُ تُرٰبًا‏(40)\nINNAA ANZARNAAKUM A’ZAABAN QAREEBAN-Y, YAWMA YANZORUL MAR-O MAA QADDAMAT YADAAHO WA YAQOOLUL KAAFERO YAA LAYTANEE KUNTO TORAABAA.\nIndeed We have warned you of a punishment near at hand—the day when a person will observe what his hands have sent ahead and the faithless one will say, ‘I wish I were dust!’",
  "merits": "There are 40 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah everyday will be fortunate enough to visit Masjidul Haraam in the same year. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that memorization of this Surah carries great reward.\nIf this Surah is recited with the intention of staying awake, then the reciter will not fall asleep and if it is recited before travelling then the journey will become easy. Drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved cures stomach problems."
